  "preamble": "A velar stop becomes the velar nasal [ŋ] before a nasal consonant. In Korean a coda /k/ is pronounced [ŋ] before a nasal onset, within words and across compound boundaries (국물 [kuŋmul] 'broth', 한국말 [hanguŋmal] 'Korean language').",
